{"name":"Olive Drab","hex":"#6f7632","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"olive drab","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A greyish green colour, like that of a ripe green olive; almost invariably with a matte finish.","Cloth of an olive drab colour, used often for military uniforms."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greyish green colour, like that of a ripe green olive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/olive_drab"}],"entries":[{"title":"Olive (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Olive, also called olive green, is a dark shade of yellowish green, like that of unripe or green olives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Olives_stuffed_with_almonds.jpg/330px-Olives_stuffed_with_almonds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive_(color)","wikidata":"Q864152"},{"title":"Drab (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Drab is a dull, light-brown color. It originally took its name from a fabric of the same color made of undyed, homespun wool. The word was first used in English in 1686. It probably originated from the Old French word drap, which meant cloth. In 1897 the Sears catalog listed household paint colors including drab, light drab, Quaker drab, and olive drab."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Beige_wool_texture.jpg/330px-Beige_wool_texture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drab_(color)","wikidata":"Q16938364"},{"title":"Olive","blocks":[{"text":"The cultivated olive is a subspecies of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. Olea europaea is the type species for its genus, Olea, which lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil was originally synonymous with olive oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Olivesfromjordan.jpg/330px-Olivesfromjordan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive","wikidata":"Q1621080"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/SR_Maunsell_saloon_%289132055782%29.jpg/500px-SR_Maunsell_saloon_%289132055782%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/SR_Maunsell_saloon_%289132055782%29.jpg/500px-SR_Maunsell_saloon_%289132055782%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASR_Maunsell_saloon_(9132055782).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/178-%D0%B9_%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1_6-%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%B2.%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1%D1%80_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BC_%D1%81%D0%BC%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B5.1981%D0%B3.JPG/500px-178-%D0%B9_%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1_6-%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%B2.%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1%D1%80_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BC_%D1%81%D0%BC%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B5.1981%D0%B3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/178-%D0%B9_%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1_6-%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%B2.%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1%D1%80_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BC_%D1%81%D0%BC%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B5.1981%D0%B3.JPG/500px-178-%D0%B9_%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1_6-%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%B2.%D0%BE%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B1%D1%80_%D0%BD%D0%B0_%D1%81%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%BC_%D1%81%D0%BC%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B5.1981%D0%B3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"htt